# An allow-list for the AgentCore image (infra/docker/Dockerfile): ignore
# everything, then name what the image needs. A deny-list would have to keep
# up with every secret and large file the repo grows (.env, the 1 GB SQLite
# seed, node_modules); an allow-list cannot leak what it never names.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!agent_app/**
!data/**
!.env.defaults
!infra/docker/entrypoint.sh
# CDK stages the context through this list before building, so the Dockerfile
# itself has to be on it; a plain `docker build` reads it from outside.
!infra/docker/Dockerfile
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
